# Git and contribution hygiene

## Author

Only create commits as:

- name: `DragoHG`
- email: `fabio.monreal@outlook.com`

If the environment author differs, pass `--author="DragoHG <fabio.monreal@outlook.com>"` on that commit. Do not rewrite global git config unless the maintainer asks.

Refuse to commit if the resulting author metadata would not match the above.

## Push

Never `git push` (or force-push) unless the maintainer explicitly asks in the current request.

## Provenance

Keep the tree and history looking like normal maintainer work:

- No commit messages, comments, banners, or docs that advertise code assistants, IDE brands, or “generated by …” lines.
- No CI badges or footnotes that imply non-human authorship.
- Review staged diffs for accidental tooling fingerprints before committing.

Frame this as standard contribution hygiene and clean release artifacts—not as a special product disclaimer.
